{{!
    @template enrol_apply/review_summary

    The strip that opens the review page: who applied, in what state, how, through which method
    and how long ago. It answers the decider's first question before any sentence is read.

    Every chip carries text beside its colour and icon; the status chip's label is visually
    hidden so a screen reader hears "Status: Deferred" and the eye reads the chip. The label and
    the value stay on one line of this template, because a Behat "I should see" matches the raw
    text.

    Context variables required for this template:
    * readonly boolean - whether the reader may only look, which earns the read-only chip
    * readonlylabel string - that chip's text
    * statuslabel string - the visually hidden label of the status chip
    * status string - whether the application is pending or on the waiting list
    * iswaiting boolean - whether it is on the waiting list, which picks the chip's icon
    * statuschipclass string - the chip's background and text colour classes, a literal pair
    * haskeychip boolean - whether the applicant presented a group enrolment key
    * keychip string - what that key did, naming its group to a reader who may see it; plain
      spelling, escaped by the double stash
    * haswaited boolean - whether the application date is known
    * waited string - how long it has waited, with the date
    * methodlabel string - label of the enrolment method
    * methodname string - the method's name, plain spelling
    * courselabel string - label of the course
    * coursename string - full name of the course applied for, plain spelling
    * courseurl string - link to the course
    * hasidentity boolean - whether this reader may see any identifying detail of the applicant
    * identity array - one entry per identity field the site named and this reader may see, each
      carrying a label and a value, both in the PLAIN spelling; the e-mail address is one of
      these when showuseridentity names it and absent when it does not
    * profileurl string - the applicant's profile in this course
    * profilelabel string - text of the profile link, a plain link rather than a button: the
      heaviest control in the first block should not be the one that leaves the page
    * hasdecision boolean - whether a colleague has already decided this one, which today means
      it was deferred
    * decisionlabel string - heading of that line
    * decision string - who deferred it and when, plain spelling
    * hasdecisionmessage boolean - whether they wrote anything to the applicant
    * decisionmessage string - what they wrote, ALREADY escaped with its line breaks converted,
      which is why it is triple stashed
    * hasdecisionnote boolean - whether they left a note for whoever reads this next
    * decisionnotelabel string - label of that note
    * decisionnote string - the note, ALREADY escaped with its line breaks converted, hence the
      triple stash. Shown here and deliberately NOT pre-filled into the note box, because that
      writer clears on empty and a pre-filled box would carry one decision's reason into the next

    Example context (json):
    {
        "readonly": true,
        "readonlylabel": "Read only",
        "statuslabel": "Status",
        "status": "Deferred",
        "iswaiting": true,
        "statuschipclass": "bg-info text-white",
        "haskeychip": true,
        "keychip": "Key accepted: Turma A",
        "haswaited": true,
        "waited": "Applied 2 days 3 hours ago (03/11/26, 09:14)",
        "methodlabel": "Method",
        "methodname": "Application with a group key",
        "courselabel": "Course",
        "coursename": "R&D < Team induction",
        "courseurl": "https://example.com/course/view.php?id=7",
        "hasidentity": true,
        "identity": [
            {"label": "Username", "value": "jsa"},
            {"label": "ID number", "value": "2026-0071"}
        ],
        "profileurl": "https://example.com/user/view.php?id=5&course=7",
        "profilelabel": "View profile",
        "hasdecision": true,
        "decisionlabel": "The decision so far",
        "decision": "Deferred by Ana Souza on 10/08/26, 14:02.",
        "hasdecisionmessage": true,
        "decisionmessage": "Waiting for the second group to open.",
        "hasdecisionnote": true,
        "decisionnotelabel": "Note for the record",
        "decisionnote": "Second intake opens in September."
    }
}}
<div class="enrol_apply-reviewstrip mb-3">
    <div class="d-flex flex-wrap align-items-center gap-2 mb-2">
        {{#readonly}}<span class="badge bg-secondary text-dark enrol_apply-chip-readonly">{{#pix}}t/hide, core{{/pix}}{{readonlylabel}}</span>{{/readonly}}
        <span class="badge {{statuschipclass}} enrol_apply-statuschip">{{^iswaiting}}<span class="enrol_apply-statusdot"></span>{{/iswaiting}}{{#iswaiting}}{{#pix}}i/duration, core{{/pix}}{{/iswaiting}}<span class="visually-hidden">{{statuslabel}}: </span>{{status}}</span>
        {{#haskeychip}}<span class="badge bg-primary text-white enrol_apply-keychip">{{#pix}}key, enrol_apply{{/pix}}{{keychip}}</span>{{/haskeychip}}
        {{#haswaited}}<span class="small text-body-secondary">{{waited}}</span>{{/haswaited}}
    </div>
    <div class="d-flex flex-wrap align-items-baseline gap-3">
        <dl class="enrol_apply-identity small text-body-secondary mb-0 d-flex flex-wrap gap-3">
            <div><dt class="d-inline fw-normal">{{methodlabel}}:</dt> <dd class="d-inline ms-1">{{methodname}}</dd></div>
            <div><dt class="d-inline fw-normal">{{courselabel}}:</dt> <dd class="d-inline ms-1"><a href="{{courseurl}}">{{coursename}}</a></dd></div>
            {{#hasidentity}}
                {{#identity}}
                    <div><dt class="d-inline fw-normal">{{label}}:</dt> <dd class="d-inline ms-1">{{value}}</dd></div>
                {{/identity}}
            {{/hasidentity}}
        </dl>
        <a class="small" href="{{profileurl}}">{{profilelabel}}</a>
    </div>
    {{#hasdecision}}
        <div class="alert alert-info mt-2 mb-0" role="status">
            <strong>{{decisionlabel}}</strong> {{decision}}
            {{#hasdecisionmessage}}<div class="mt-1">{{{decisionmessage}}}</div>{{/hasdecisionmessage}}
            {{#hasdecisionnote}}
                <div class="mt-1"><strong>{{decisionnotelabel}}:</strong> {{{decisionnote}}}</div>
            {{/hasdecisionnote}}
        </div>
    {{/hasdecision}}
</div>
